# Descriptor for this agent. Deliberately empty of declarations.
#
# agent-mgr derives everything from the REGISTRY NAME, and for `property` every
# default is already what this agent runs: AGENT_HOME ~/.hermes-property,
# AGENT_CONTAINER hermes-property, AGENT_PROJECT hermes-property, and
# AGENT_CONFIG config.yaml beside this file.
#
# Declaring any of them would pin this repo to one person. A repo that declares
# AGENT_HOME cannot be shared at all -- agent-mgr's require_own_home refuses the
# second instance, because it resolves to the first one's home. Leaving the
# descriptor bare is what lets a second person register their own row against
# their own checkout and get their own home, container and project.
#
# Per-person values that are NOT identity -- a different Mac, a different model
# -- belong in ~/.hermes-<name>/.env and reach config.yaml as ${VAR}, which the
# gateway interpolates at runtime. mcp_servers.latch below already works that
# way. AGENT_TZ is the exception, because Compose renders TZ before the gateway
# ever reads the file.
